pr: n5
title: JVM: Phase 5 -- encode coverage to 96.5% and the classlib registry
branch: pr/05-phase5-encode-coverage

# nqp section N8 (Phase 5 encode-coverage campaign): log lines 233..285,
# 53 commits. No docs-only commits in this range, so no lab-notebook group.
# Engine machinery, encoder batches and the registry all touch NqpOps.java
# and TruffleEncoder.nqp, so every group is a contiguous run; nothing moved.

= Phase 5: calling-convention family; a coverage report that cannot lie
The calling-convention ops encode; repeat loops encode and immediate blocks
must not; the encode decision is traceable, and the coverage report counts
blocks the way the encoder actually decides them.
- 01649f700 Phase 5: the calling-convention family, and a coverage report that cannot lie
- 2bdcefe89 Phase 5: repeat loops encode; immediate blocks must not; the encode decision is traceable

= Phase 5: sole blockers, op desugars, list constructors -- 70.7% -> 81.7%
Two sole-blocker batches (CORE.c 70.7% -> 74.2% of blocks), encoding through
the registered op desugars (-> 77.3%), the list constructors (-> 80.6%) and
native attribute references (-> 81.7%). hlllist/hllhash read the running
frame's HLL config.
- ece3b0c8b Phase 5: the sole-blocker batch -- CORE.c goes 70.7% -> 73.4% of blocks
- a710fd6a8 Phase 5: second sole-blocker batch -- CORE.c 73.4% -> 74.2% of blocks
- e0003e7cd Code engine: hlllist/hllhash read the running frame's HLL config
- 5abb4ac44 Phase 5: encode through registered op desugars -- CORE.c 74.2% -> 77.3%
- cdfb2545e Phase 5: the list constructors encode -- CORE.c 77.8% -> 80.6% of blocks
- 23f247c1d Phase 5: native attribute references encode -- CORE.c 80.6% -> 81.7% of blocks

= Code engine: dispatch programs replay as PE-visible code; JDK out of PE
Dispatch programs replay as partial-evaluation-visible code and enter engine
callees directly; the JDK stays out of partial evaluation; attribute reads
compile to field loads.
- aaa67257a Code engine: dispatch programs replay as PE-visible code, and enter engine callees directly
- 8bd9b1c42 Code engine: keep the JDK out of partial evaluation; attribute reads as field loads

= keep
- 06ced76b2 Phase 5: the typed assigns encode

= Code engine: instruction caches, lazy refold, inlining across dispatch
Per-instruction caches for lexical-by-name, WVal and attribute access; the
caller chain is searched for a live outer only when one can exist; Kotlin's
null and lateinit checks stay out of compiled code; the interpreter loop is
handed Truffle exceptions, never host ones; a dispatch site refolds lazily,
not on every install; engine callees inline across a dispatch through
adopted call nodes.
- 814a5e4b1 Code engine: per-instruction caches for lexical-by-name, WVal, and attribute access
- 6f1f93aaa JVM: search the caller chain for a live outer only when one can exist
- bc7bfd2a3 Code engine: keep Kotlin's null and lateinit checks out of compiled code
- 0aa75dded Code engine: hand the interpreter loop Truffle exceptions, never host ones
- 4b8de20a5 Code engine: refold a dispatch site lazily, not on every install
- ad4f7e8b8 Code engine: engine callees inline across a dispatch through adopted call nodes

= Code engine: lexicalrefs, the exception family, defor, native parameters
Native lexical references encode (the lexicalref scope); the exception
family, typed attributes, the valued two-child if and the small sole
blockers; Raku's own defor, not nqp's; native parameters and immediate
blocks, with the three encoder bugs they exposed fixed.
- 0260f5ac4 Code engine: native lexical references encode (the lexicalref scope)
- 61744899f Code engine: the exception family, typed attributes, valued two-child if, and the small sole blockers
- 62a87e1ca Code engine: Raku's own defor, not nqp's
- 8cc46ca6a Code engine: native parameters, immediate blocks, and three encoder bugs they exposed

= Code engine: small-op tranches, loop bodies, uint lexicals, regex, hash
Tranches of small ops plus a host-exception diagnostic; loop bodies that
take the condition; plain uint lexicals share the int slots; an
engine-covered regex encodes, handed to the grammar engine; a flat named
argument carries no name, and hash encodes; the mechanical tail: multidim,
floor/ceil, objectid, ord/rindex/index arity desugars, pow_I,
ctxcallerskipthunks, multidim refs.
- a38ac6bb6 Code engine: a tranche of small ops, and a host-exception diagnostic
- 610001737 Code engine: loop bodies that take the condition, and more small ops
- 89d2a2ab2 Code engine: plain uint lexicals share the int slots
- a1c5fc578 Code engine: an engine-covered regex encodes, handed to the grammar engine
- 905134017 Code engine: a flat named argument carries no name, and hash encodes
- d2370d749 Code engine: the small-op mechanical tail (multidim, floor/ceil, objectid, and kin)
- e31086efb Code engine: ord/rindex/index arity desugars, pow_I, ctxcallerskipthunks, multidim refs

= Truffle encoder: with/without, uint params and attrs, op sweeps -> 96.5%
with/without and the pure op tail (95.3%); uint parameters and comparisons
with the atomic/IO tail (95.6%); uint attributes, Math ops and the IO/misc
tail (96.0%); the computational op sweep, then p6return as the SUCCEED
handler's value (96.5%).
- b79ff0643 Truffle encoder: with/without + pure op tail -> 95.3%
- 60fa74be3 Truffle encoder: uint parameters + uint comparisons + atomic/IO tail -> 95.6%
- 7ad7878ce Truffle encoder: uint attributes + Math ops + IO/misc tail -> 96.0%
- 86410afcf Truffle encoder: computational op sweep -> 96.5%
- ed84c2fa6 Truffle encoder: p6return as the SUCCEED handler's value -> 96.5%

= Truffle encoder: syscall dispatch, IO::Path op rows, uint boxes unsigned
nqp::syscall encodes as the boot-syscall dispatch it is, with the stat
syscall family; an immediate block's `count` alone no longer bails (+7 net:
each given/when routine it frees is refused again by loop shape, chained
chain or resume); the file/env op rows the un-guarded IO::Path code needs;
P6opaque's atomic attribute ops delegate like the plain ones; a uint result
boxes through box_u, and a native uint boxes and unboxes unsigned. 96.5%.
- e4e02c345 Truffle: nqp::syscall as the boot-syscall dispatch it is; the stat syscall family
- 16efe3810 Truffle encoder: an immediate block's `count` alone does not bail -> 96.5%
- eff7c4537 Truffle encoder: the file/env op rows the un-guarded IO::Path code needs
- 1ea99c3e1 P6opaque: the atomic attribute ops delegate like the plain ones
- 9c0ef460f Truffle encoder: a uint result type that boxes through box_u -> 96.5%
- eeb23686f Runtime: a native uint boxes and unboxes unsigned

